t.com/u/194539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov","html_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1912,"digest":"sha256:c0ff3fa36eb993b6db53438bf63a128473582571a534a255aafe304becff548f","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-09-17T11:09:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T11:09:21Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/download/v0.60.2/verification.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/tarball/v0.60.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/zipball/v0.60.2","body":"# v0.60.2 — Practice and Playground readability\n\nThis package records the reviewed P05 Practice and Playground readability source scope below. Its actual qualification and original frozen payload evidence are attached. Affected player journeys and phase acceptance require separate public verification; this package does not claim completion of the music rollout, physical-device certification or later phases.\n\nReviewed P05 source scope: practice and playground readability, shared display preferences, history selector restoration, editor undo focus, current viewport diagnostics.\n\nExact game source: `ece40093940aabdc3b3659a07394b856f33ad4a1` (tree `32b36e6e8fc605911b2cb98cd8f67c97b8f4e214`).\n\nAll six source gates passed through the hosted exact-source workflow. Each of the two complete four-shard families passed 5,449 tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs. Production reproduction/readiness and the ordinary build passed on the hosted source. Both hosted source families used Node 20.19.6. No local command gates are claimed by this qualification pipeline; earlier local P05 cohorts remain separately source-scoped corroboration. The full test suite and ordinary build use the actual hosted authority above; no duplicate local execution is claimed.\n\nThe separately authenticated hosted utility inspected the complete frozen original artifact. Its source archive matches all 8,806 tracked files and modes. Every one of the 682 game files matches its original manifest. Local assembly rehashes the retained original metadata and preserves exact runner member descriptors for the source and distribution payloads; it does not download or rehash the large originals locally. The attached evidence preserves the selected original qualification and Practice and Playground observations, including retained earlier failures; it does not replace verification of this release after deployment.\n\nPredecessor: [v0.60.1](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/tag/v0.60.1). Before current selector cutover, integrate the root-reviewed Archive11 successor preserving original v0.60.1 and all v0.51.0 canonical bytes. The complete public audit and scoped native journeys passed. Preserve all 14 predecessor pins, other archive owners and current catalog rows; no previous release is rebuilt or overwritten. Complete the normal main publisher PR/merge, deployed byte verification and applicable native play/offline evidence. Source and attachment qualification alone do not establish public P05 acceptance.\n\nAt package assembly, public byte/play/offline verification is pending; acceptance is recorded separately after publication. Full P05 remains incomplete. Modeled input, browser observations and physical-device qualification remain separate evidence categories.\n"}